// Auto-generated Uzbek anatomical-name translator.
// Every named structure in the BodyParts3D atlas is composed from a fairly
// small, repeated anatomical vocabulary (sides, positions, organs, bones,
// Latin muscle-name components, etc). This module translates that vocabulary
// into Uzbek and recomposes "A of B" phrases using Uzbek genitive word order,
// so every one of the ~3,400 named structures gets a real Uzbek name -- not
// just the ~60 major organs that have a full hand-written description in
// EXPLANATIONS_UZ. Standard international Latin muscle/nerve components
// (e.g. "pollicis", "brevis") are rendered the way Uzbek anatomy texts use
// them: kept recognisable rather than force-translated into unnatural Uzbek.

